            <ArticleTitle>Painful bone end sclerosis. Variant of renal osteodystrophy simulating osteonecrosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>171-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Painless sclerotic change in bone ends occurring as a manifestation of renal osteodystrophy has been reported in two previous cases. The sclerotic change can, however, be accompanied by nonspecific periarticular pain. Radiologic changes in &quot;bone ends&quot; may mimic osteonecrosis. Nuclear bone scanning may show increased radionuclide uptake early in both conditions but late uptake may be less in &quot;bone end sclerosis.&quot; The &quot;rugger jersey&quot; spine occurring in the usual osteosclerosis of renal osteodystrophy has been consistently absent in this variant. Osteonecrosis should be excluded in making the diagnosis of &quot;bone end sclerosis.&quot;</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
